  "body": "Found while fixing #1631 (PR #1634). Read from the code; not reproduced by a run yet.\n\nWhat happens: #1631 gives a stock-source Drill (no cross holes), Bore and Thread the containment law against the setup's parts (`keep_law::is_hole_kind`, `parts_in_stock`). A Drill WITH cross holes is left out. Its chain is judged by `cross_part::part_clear`, which reads `material.facets`, the source's mesh (`generate.rs`, the `cross_spindle::cross_drill` call). On a stock source that is the stock, not the parts held in it. So a cross hole off the stock that enters a part may have no op finding. The cross chain is posed, so the program sim refuses to judge it. Whether such a program then posts, or is refused another way (the stock read as the solid to keep), is the open question.\n\nExpected: a stock-source cross drill that enters a part is a blocking finding on the op, or is refused by name. A cross hole through stock-only material, or into a cross hole the part models, stays legal.\n\nOpen design point: the containment law in `contain_into` excuses vertical hole walls only (`HoleAxis::vertical`). A cross chain needs each hole's own axis, as `cross_part::walls` builds them.\n\nDone means: a test with a stock-source cross drill into a part, and one into stock-only material, shows a blocking finding or a named refusal for the first, and the second still posts or is refused only for a stated reason.\n\nPart of the #1607 / #1631 stock-source law.\n",
